litteraturlista/
*.gdoc

# Third-party course material downloaded from Canvas: KTH templates, grading criteria,
# detailed plans, seminar slides and other students' example theses. This repository and
# the site built from it are public, so none of it belongs in git. The vault keeps the
# files locally; the audit and the linter skip the folder.
**/Filer/Canvas/

# Text-extractor plugin OCR cache: derived data regenerated on demand, not authored
# content, and nothing a public repo should carry.
.obsidian/plugins/text-extractor/cache/

# Get-SRIntegrity.ps1's pre-sweep snapshot. Transient by design: taken immediately before a
# bulk edit and consumed immediately after, so a committed copy would be stale the moment it
# lands and would dirty the tree on every use.
Meta/Obsidian Plugins/Scripts/sr-baseline.json

# Per-device Obsidian config folder for the phone, selected there with Settings >
# "Override config folder" so mobile does not load the desktop's plugin set. It is state
# for one device and recreatable, so it is not tracked - unlike .obsidian/, which is
# deliberately committed as a restore point. Note that if a plugin installed there ever
# ships a .md file, both .markdownlint-cli2.jsonc and Vault-Audit.ps1's InScope would need
# the same exclusion they give .obsidian/: neither one matches .obsidian-mobile, because
# both test for a path segment that ends exactly at ".obsidian". See F75 and current-state.
.obsidian-mobile/
